    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. The endpoint is defined by `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 an 11-step OfficeFloor pipeline (no Spring controller exists). Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end. The file also declares `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`, but `petclinic.security.enable=false` in `application.properties`, so that guard is inert in the default profile.\n\nOne important framework detail up front: the body is bound in step 1 as `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` **without `@Valid`**, so the DTO's Bean-Validation annotations (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`) are **not** enforced. Only the hand-written checks below run.\n\n## Validations and side-effects, in order\n\n1. **`BuildOwner`** (reads the body \u2014 the only step that does)\n   - *Validation:* required non-blank check on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`. Any blank/missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing them \u2192 **400** `{errors:[...]}`.\n   - *Side-effects:* maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today) rolled forward to the next business day (Sat\u2192+2, Sun\u2192+1).\n\n2. **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`**\n   - *Validation:* postcode is optional (null \u2192 skip). If present, must be exactly 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException([\"postcode\"])` \u2192 **400**.\n\n3. **`NormalizeOwnerAddress`**\n   - *Validation:* address blank after trim \u2192 **400** (`[\"address\"]`).\n   - *Side-effect:* mutates `Owner` in place \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE.\n\n4. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n   - *Validation:* telephone must convert to E.164 (assumes +61 if no country code, enforces digit-count rules); unconvertible \u2192 **400** (`[\"telephone\"]`).\n   - *Side-effect:* rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place.\n\n5. **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`**\n   - *Validation:* email optional (null/blank \u2192 skip). If present must match the email regex, else \u2192 **400** (`[\"email\"]`).\n   - *Side-effect:* lower-cases `email` in place.\n\n6. **`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`**\n   - *Validation:* scans all owners; if another has the same normalized telephone **and** email \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**. (Read side-effect: `ownerRepository.findAll()`.)\n\n7. **`RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`**\n   - *Validation:* if the city (trimmed, case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n8. **`RejectOwnerDailyLimit`**\n   - *Validation:* if \u2265 100 existing owners already share the new owner's `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n9. **`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`**\n   - *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (owners in that city by exact string match) + 1, zero-padded.\n\n10. **`SaveOwner`**\n    - *Side-effect:* `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (persists), then writes an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate.\n\n11. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n    - *Side-effect:* maps `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`, enriches with computed `namesakeCount`, `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning` (plus mapper-injected `displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `membershipNumber`), and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notable gaps / inconsistencies in the current code\n- **DTO validation is dead code:** because step 1 omits `@Valid`, all the `@NotNull`/`@Pattern`/`@Size` constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto` (including the name-format patterns and length caps) never run \u2014 only the manual blank-check does. This diverges from the `@Valid` pattern in AGENTS.md.\n- **City counting is inconsistent:** the capacity check (step 7) compares city case-insensitively/trimmed, but the customer-code sequence (step 9) uses exact string `equals`, so the two can disagree.\n- **`sharesHousehold`** is accepted by the DTO but consulted by no step; the duplicate check keys only on telephone+email.\n\nEffective URL is `POST http://localhost:9966/petclinic/api/owners` (the `/petclinic` comes from `server.servlet.context-path`, the `/api` from the directory layout)."
  },
